    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d502">

                <pb facs="0805" n="701" sameAs="frus:frus1933v02/pg701"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">852.75 National Telephone Company/169:
                    Telegram</note>
                <head>
                    <hi rendition="#italic">The Chargé in Spain (Flack) to the Secretary of State
                    </hi>
                </head>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right">
                        <placeName>
                            <hi rendition="#small-caps">Madrid</hi></placeName>, <date
                            calendar="gregorian" when="1933-05-15T15:00:00+00:00">May 15, 1933—3
                            p.m.</date>
                        <lb/> [Received May 15—1:25 p.m.]</dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>20. Learn from Rock that he has sent important communications to his principals
                    concerning indirect efforts to impair telephone contract.</p>
                <p>In the absence of specific instructions I shall reiterate our position enunciated
                    last year<anchor n="16" xml:id="d502-f1"/> should action be required.</p>
                <closer>
                    <signed>
                        <hi rendition="#small-caps">Flack</hi>
                    </signed>
                </closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
    <standOff>
        <listAnnotation>
            <note corresp="#d502-f1" n="16" xml:id="d502-f1-content">
                <p>See telegram No. 90, November 23, 1932, from the Ambassador in Spain, <ref
                        target="frus1932v02#pg_566">
                        <hi rendition="#italic">Foreign Relations</hi>, 1932, vol. <hi
                            rendition="#small-caps">ii</hi>, p. 566</ref>.</p>
            </note>
